  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Caterpillar India Workers Union vs The Director Of Industrial Safety And ... on 15 April, 2025 Author: M.Dhandapani Bench: M.Dhandapani W In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated: 15-04-2025 Coram The Honourable Mr Justice M.Dhandapani Wp No. 5921 of 2023 And Wmp No. 5919 Of 2023 1.",
    "facts": "The present writ petition has been filed seeking a direction to the 3rd respondent to run the canteen meant for the workers in the premises allotted for the purpose in the factory including Cooking of the food in the said kitchen of the canteen and further direct the 1st and 2nd respondent to ensure such compliance by the 3rd respondent. 2. It is the case of the petitioner that the third respondent management which employs about 3000 workers in its factory at Melnallathur Village, Thiruvallur has statutory duty to run a canteen in accordance with section 46 of https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis However, the third respondent management has not provided the canteen as mandated under the Act and they have provided pre-cooked food from outside and served to the workers which is inadequate quality and quantity. Therefore, the petitioner Union made a complaint before the respondents 1 & 2 and the same has not been considered. Hence, the present writ petition. 3. The Party-in-person appearing for the petitioner Union submitted that based on the complaint, the respondents 1 & 2 have initiated the proceedings as against the respondents 3 & 4 on 18.01.2023 and subsequently, a criminal case has also been filed in Cr. Nos.674 and 678 of 2023 as the respondents 3 & 4 and the same is pending.",
